NGINX WEBSITE DEPLOYMENT USING DOCKER WITHOUT ALPINE

1.  docker –version
    -   Verifies that Docker is installed and displays its version.
2.  mkdir mysite
    -   Creates a new directory to store website files.
3.  cd mysite
    -   Navigates into the website project directory.
4.  echo “
    Hello from Nginx
    ” > index.html
    -   Creates a simple HTML file to be served by Nginx.
5.  sudo docker run -d -p 8080:80 -v $(pwd):/usr/share/nginx/html nginx
    -   Runs an Nginx container in detached mode, maps port 8080 to 80,
        and mounts the current directory as the web root.
6.  sudo docker ps
    -   Displays running Docker containers to confirm Nginx is active.
7.  ip a
    -   Displays the system IP address to access the Nginx site from a
        browser.
8.  sudo docker stop $(sudo docker ps -q)
    -   Stops all running Docker containers if the port is already in
        use.
9.  sudo docker rm $(sudo docker ps -aq)
    -   Removes all Docker containers for a clean restart if needed.

NGINX + NODE 18 ALPINE DEPLOYMENT 

1.  cd ~
    -   Navigates to the home directory to safely create the project
        folder.
2.  pwd
    -   Displays the current working directory to confirm location.
3.  mkdir nginx-node-app
    -   Creates a new project directory for the Nginx Docker
        application.
4.  cd nginx-node-app
    -   Enters the project directory.
5.  nano index.html
    -   Creates and edits the HTML file that will be served by Nginx.
6.  nano Dockerfile
    -   Creates and edits the Dockerfile to define the multi-stage Node
        Alpine and Nginx build process.
7.  sudo docker build -t nginx-node-app .
    -   Builds the Docker image from the Dockerfile and tags it as
        ‘nginx-node-app’.
8.  sudo docker images
    -   Displays all available Docker images to confirm successful image
        creation.
9.  sudo docker run -d -p 8083:80 –name nginx-container nginx-node-app
    -   Runs the container in detached mode, mapping host port 8083 to
        container port 80.
10. sudo docker ps
    -   Displays running containers to verify that the Nginx container
        is active.
